# Old Redleaf — forest T2 basic striker (HP 18, basic moves + limited deadly attack)

[title Old Redleaf]
[image monsters/forest_bear.png]
[stats hp=18]
[trigger road]

* move Attack
  narration: It swipes a forepaw at you, claws splayed.
  narration: It bats at your guard, testing.

* move Defend
  narration: It hunches and turns its shoulder to absorb the blow.

* move Recover
  narration: It steps back and shakes its head, clearing the daze.

* move Heavy Slow Telegraphed Attack
  narration: It rears onto its hind legs and brings both forepaws down hard.

* intro
You hear it first: the snap of brush thirty paces upslope, then the wet
huff of breath. It comes down through the trees without hurry. Massive,
grizzled, the fur at its shoulders silvered. When it stops to look at you,
its eyes catch the canopy-light wrong, an ember-glow that holds steady when
it shouldn't. The forest has gone quiet around you both.

* win
+give_gold 10
+add_tag killed_old_redleaf
The bear settles in the leaves and does not rise again. Whatever held the
ember-glow behind its eyes has gone out. The forest, slow to remember it
was a forest, begins to make small noises again.

* lose
The world tips sideways. Somewhere, a long way off, the forest starts
breathing again without you.
